PROBE 1, the predecessor's MANDATORY step-1 hypothesis, VERBATIM as it was written, and NEGATIVE on its own stated falsifier. Added before the loop --
    u32* t1 = lbl_80240FB0;
    u32* t2 = lbl_80240FA0;
and rewrote the two stores as `... = t1[i];` / `... = t2[i];`. Result: MWCC hoists BOTH address materialisations out of the loop, COUNT PARITY IS LOST (T141/O139, `probe.py` prints the class change explicitly), real 32 -> 104, opcode multiset 2t -> 8t, and the +0x74/+0x78 pair does not swap. The hypothesis named this exact outcome as its cheapest refuting observation.
PROBE 2, the natural counter-form, NEGATIVE and WORSE THAN NEUTRAL. Swapped the two store statements so the tbl2 (lbl_80240FA0) store precedes the tbl1 (lbl_80240FB0) one --
        *(u32*)((u8*)b + i * 4 + offsetof(DiagPadLatch, tbl2)) = lbl_80240FA0[i];
        *(u32*)((u8*)b + i * 4 + offsetof(DiagPadLatch, tbl1)) = lbl_80240FB0[i];
Count parity is regained (141/141) but real goes 32 -> 36 and, decisively, TWO IMMEDIATE divergences appear that no postprocessor class may ever close: +0xa0 ours `stw r0,32(r9)` against the target's `stw r0,16(r6)`, and +0xa8 ours `stw r0,16(r9)` against `stw r0,32(r6)`. The raw word count stays 18 while the SERVABLE fraction of it drops, which is the useful form of the finding: the original store order is the target's, and the emission order of the two ADDR16_LO `addi`s is not carried by it. Both probes discarded with `probe.py --discard`; src/game/pb/pb_diag.c is byte-identical to HEAD.
